@startuml
title TTC cookie connection selection and fallback
hide footbox
participant Connector as C
participant "Instantiator factory" as F
participant "Cookie instantiator" as I
participant "Cookie negotiator" as N
participant "Cookie authenticator" as A
participant MessageStreamer as S
participant "Normal instantiator" as Normal
database "Oracle Database" as DB

note over C,DB
The network session is already established.
Without an eligible cache hit, the factory selects normal connection setup.
end note
C -> F : select(config, networkSession, reneg=false)
F --> C : cookie instantiator for eligible cache hit
C -> I : GetConnection(ctx)
I -> N : Negotiate(ctx)
N -> S : queue TTIPRO + TTICOOKIE + TTIDTY
N -> S : register DTY decode callbacks
N --> I : session context and shelf
I -> I : prepare authentication dependencies
I -> A : Authenticate(ctx)
alt Password
    A -> S : Push(OSESSKEY)
else Token
    A -> S : Push(OAUTH)
end
A -> S : Flush(ctx)
S -> DB : queued negotiation + first authentication request

alt Cookie accepted
    loop Read delayed negotiation and authentication responses
        DB --> S : next TTC message
        A -> S : Pull(ctx, expected types)
        S -> S : select payload marshaller by message type
        opt TTIDTY
            S -> N : prepare DTY decoder; store time-zone version after decode
        end
        S --> A : decoded message or error
    end
    A -> A : validate OER and required RPA; update session properties
    opt Password: complete OAUTH after OSESSKEY
        A -> S : send OAUTH through shared password setup
        S -> DB : OAUTH
        DB --> S : OAUTH responses
        S --> A : authentication result
    end
    A --> I : success
    I -> S : remove cookie DTY callbacks
    I --> C : constructed connection
else Server requests TTIRENEG
    DB --> S : TTIRENEG; replacement TTIPRO follows
    S --> A : TTIRENEG
    A --> I : ErrTTIRENEG
    I -> S : remove cookie DTY callbacks
    I --> C : ErrTTIRENEG
    C -> F : select(config, same networkSession, reneg=true)
    F --> C : normal instantiator in recovery mode
    C -> Normal : GetConnection(ctx)
    note over Normal,DB
    Read pending server PRO; exchange DTY; refresh eligible cache.
    Then run normal password/token authentication.
    No new network connection or second client PRO request.
    end note
    Normal --> C : connection or error
end
note over C,DB
Other errors do not trigger optimized-to-normal fallback.
Unsuccessful connection establishment disconnects the network session.
end note
@enduml
